1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
POLA-REPORT — Marketing analytics platform for Polarad ad agency

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Used only by approved agency staff to view client ad performance

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Server-to-server architecture using a System User access token

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Scene 2 — How a client grants POLA-REPORT access to their assets

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The advertiser opens our login page and clicks "Continue with Meta"

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Facebook displays the consent screen for all five requested permissions

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:00,000
ads_read, ads_management, business_management, pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
After consent we exchange the code and store a long-lived token (60 days)

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Alternative — the client can grant permissions in Business Manager directly

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Business Settings → Apps → Add → POLA-REPORT → Assign assets

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Scene 3 — The /meta hub lists all five permissions with live status

12
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Each card connects to a demo page that exercises one permission end-to-end

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Scene 4 — pages_show_list

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Calls GET /me/accounts to list Pages the user manages

15
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Used to map each client to the correct Facebook Page in their setup

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Scene 5 — pages_read_engagement

17
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Reads Page-level aggregate insights: followers, page likes, impressions, engaged users

18
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Displayed alongside paid ad performance for a unified report

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Scene 6 — business_management

20
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Calls GET /me/businesses and reads owned_ad_accounts and owned_pages

21
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Keeps the client → ad-account mapping in sync as assets are added or removed

22
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Scene 7 — ads_read

23
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Reads ad-account status, currency, amount spent and campaign-level insights

24
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:54,000
This is the data behind every KPI card on the client dashboard

25
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Now switching to the live dashboard for client hea-pangyo

26
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Impressions, clicks, spend, CTR — all derived from the ads_read API call above

27
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Scene 8 — ads_management

28
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:40,000
The operator can pause an under-performing campaign without leaving the dashboard

29
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Clicking Pause issues POST /v22.0/{campaign_id} with status PAUSED

30
00:04:52,000 --> 00:05:04,000
The UI updates immediately to reflect the new status returned by the API

31
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Clicking Activate reverses the action — POST status ACTIVE

32
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:28,000
ads_management is used only for status flips, never for budget or creative changes

33
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:36,000
All Meta data is fetched server-to-server with a System User token

34
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:48,000
End customers never authenticate with Facebook through this application

35
00:05:48,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Privacy Policy: https://report.polarad.co.kr/privacy

36
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Data Deletion: https://report.polarad.co.kr/data-deletion

37
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Thank you for the review
